  "clarifications": [
    "The negative-product add0x7fff implements signed truncation, not making arbitrary values positive. For15-bit raw and byte Y/Brave the scaled products are nonnegative and at most8355585.",
    "Range1..Y presumes Y>0; zero Y still yields factor1. Likewise zero target Brave produces a scaled0 draw, not an empty-range exception. Zero Brave is outside current managed admission.",
    "The BNE after Pass/Fail skips knockback for nonzero return; zero falls through. Equality never triggers the call.",
    "The damage store runs for preview/AI too, despite the action-mode branch. Those modes consume no raw draws inside this helper; preceding evasion has its own draw contract."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "No early test for zero damage, a lethal outcome or an impossible landing before the three execution draws.",
    "Successful comparison calls knockback calculation, not guaranteed movement. That helper may reject target count, flags, mount/self/position or landing.",
    "This helper does not cap damage at999 or apply HP/live movement. It assigns type and stored damage, then may stage knockback work.",
    "Current neutral signed-safe physical formula and rules agree with the admitted path. No new physical modifiers, arbitrary signed-result settlement, general knockback or owner content is activated."
  ],
